# Financial Accounting Modules Architecture

This document defines the core Financial Accounting modules that form the baseline of the Financial Intelligence Platform before expanding into Cost Accounting and FP&A.

## Core Financial Accounting Modules

| Module Name | Core Responsibility | ERP Bridge & Validation Function |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **General Ledger (GL)** | Chart of Accounts, Journal Entry Drafts, Trial Balance | Enforces double-entry balance, mapping to standard COA |
| **Accounts Payable (AP)** | Supplier Invoices, PO Matching, Payment Drafts | 4-Way matching, duplicate detection, tax extraction |
| **Accounts Receivable (AR)** | Customer Invoices, Receipts, Credit Control | Revenue recognition rules, customer ledger reconciliation |
| **Inventory Accounting** | Stock Valuation, Landed Costs, GR/IR Clearing, COGS | Recalculates FIFO/WAV, GR/IR accrual reconciliation |
| **Cash & Bank** | Bank Reconciliation, Treasury Flow, Cash Movement | Bank statement auto-reconciliation and variance detection |
| **Fixed Assets** | Asset Register, Depreciation Schedules | Automated monthly depreciation entry calculation |
| **Tax & ZATCA Compliance** | VAT Calculation, Tax Ledger, ZATCA Rules | Tax rate validation, gross/net recalculation, audit logs |
| **Financial Closing** | Period End Control, Closing Adjustments | Trial Balance balance checks, unposted draft escalation |

## Operational Philosophy
All modules process data autonomously, perform deterministic validation via Python, and present approved drafts for human verification prior to ERP posting.
